-- 7 U.S.C. 2013: establishment of the supplemental nutrition assistance program.
-- SOURCE: usc07-ch51.txt (a converter's rendering, not the official text).
-- Percentages are NUMBERs of percent (6 means 6 percent). Seams taken as inputs: s 2025(c)(2) (the payment error rate), s 2027 (funds), s 2016(h) and s 2015(d) are not read here.
-- ANSWERS this module gives the family: `s 2013(b)(2)(B) the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently administering the distribution` (s 2012(s) asks it).

§ `s 2013(a)(1) Establishment`

-- src:143 | Subject to the availability of funds appropriated under section 2027 of this title, the Secretary is authorized to formulate and administer a supplemental nutrition assistance program under which, at the request of the State agency, eligible households within the State shall be provided an opportunity to obtain a more nutritious diet through the issuance to them of an allotment, except that a State may not participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the Secretary determines that State or local sales taxes are collected within that State on purchases of food made with benefits issued under this chapter.
@ref s 2013(a)(1), first sentence (src:143)
GIVEN `funds appropriated under section 2027 are available` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the State agency has requested the program` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the household is an eligible household within the State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Secretary determines that State or local sales taxes are collected within the State on purchases of food made with benefits issued under this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2013(a)(1) the eligible household is provided an opportunity to obtain a more nutritious diet through the issuance of an allotment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the Secretary determines that State or local sales taxes are collected within the State on purchases of food made with benefits issued under this chapter`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a State may not participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the Secretary determines that State or local sales taxes are collected within that State on purchases of food made with benefits issued under this chapter"
        IF `funds appropriated under section 2027 are available` AND `the State agency has requested the program` AND `the household is an eligible household within the State`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "at the request of the State agency, eligible households within the State shall be provided an opportunity to obtain a more nutritious diet through the issuance to them of an allotment"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the grant is "subject to the availability of funds", "at the request of the State agency", and for "eligible households within the State"

-- src:143 | Subject to the availability of funds appropriated under section 2027 of this title, the Secretary is authorized to formulate and administer a supplemental nutrition assistance program under which, at the request of the State agency, eligible households within the State shall be provided an opportunity to obtain a more nutritious diet through the issuance to them of an allotment, except that a State may not participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the Secretary determines that State or local sales taxes are collected within that State on purchases of food made with benefits issued under this chapter. The benefits so received by such households shall be used only to purchase food from retail food stores which have been approved for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program. Benefits issued and used as provided in this chapter shall be redeemable at face value by the Secretary through the facilities of the Treasury of the United States.
@ref s 2013(a)(1), second sentence (src:143)
GIVEN `the purchase is of food` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase is from a retail food store which has been approved for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2013(a)(1) the benefits may be used for the purchase` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT (`the purchase is of food` AND `the purchase is from a retail food store which has been approved for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program`)
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be used only to purchase food from retail food stores which have been approved for participation"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "only" names who and what is outside; it does not say that every purchase of food from an approved store is allowed

-- src:143 | Subject to the availability of funds appropriated under section 2027 of this title, the Secretary is authorized to formulate and administer a supplemental nutrition assistance program under which, at the request of the State agency, eligible households within the State shall be provided an opportunity to obtain a more nutritious diet through the issuance to them of an allotment, except that a State may not participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program if the Secretary determines that State or local sales taxes are collected within that State on purchases of food made with benefits issued under this chapter. The benefits so received by such households shall be used only to purchase food from retail food stores which have been approved for participation in the supplemental nutrition assistance program. Benefits issued and used as provided in this chapter shall be redeemable at face value by the Secretary through the facilities of the Treasury of the United States.
@ref s 2013(a)(1), third sentence (src:143)
GIVEN `the benefits are issued and used as provided in this chapter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2013(a)(1) the benefits are redeemable at face value by the Secretary through the facilities of the Treasury` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the benefits are issued and used as provided in this chapter`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Benefits issued and used as provided in this chapter shall be redeemable at face value by the Secretary through the facilities of the Treasury of the United States"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for benefits "issued and used as provided in this chapter"

§ `s 2013(a)(2) State quality control incentive`

DECLARE `s 2013(a)(2) payment error rate of a year` HAS
    `s 2013(a)(2) the fiscal year`                    IS A NUMBER
    `s 2013(a)(2) the payment error rate, in percent` IS A NUMBER

DECLARE `s 2013(a)(2) shares` HAS
    `s 2013(a)(2) the Federal share of the cost of the allotment, in percent` IS A NUMBER
    `s 2013(a)(2) the State share of the cost of the allotment, in percent`   IS A NUMBER

-- (A): the term "payment error rate" has the meaning given in section 2025(c)(2); that meaning is another part's, so the rates are taken as inputs.
-- src:146 | In this paragraph, the term “payment error rate” has the meaning given the term in section 2025(c)(2) of this title.
@ref s 2013(a)(2)(A), definition (src:146)
GIVEN rates IS A LIST OF `s 2013(a)(2) payment error rate of a year`
      year IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2013(a)(2)(A) the payment error rate of the State for the fiscal year` MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN r YIELD r's `s 2013(a)(2) the fiscal year` EQUALS year) rates
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the payment error rate has "the meaning given the term in section 2025(c)(2)" and was not supplied for the year
        WHEN r FOLLOWED BY rest THEN JUST (r's `s 2013(a)(2) the payment error rate, in percent`)

-- src:156 | For fiscal year 2028, to calculate the applicable State share under clause (i), a State may elect to use the payment error rate of the State from fiscal year 2025 or 2026.
@ref s 2013(a)(2)(B)(ii)(I), fiscal year 2028 (src:156)
GIVEN rates IS A LIST OF `s 2013(a)(2) payment error rate of a year`
      `the fiscal year the State elects to use the payment error rate of, if it has elected` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(ii)(I) the payment error rate the State elects to use for fiscal year 2028` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fiscal year the State elects to use the payment error rate of, if it has elected`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the State "may elect" and has not, and the clause does not say which of fiscal year 2025 or 2026 is used then
        WHEN JUST y THEN
            BRANCH
                IF y EQUALS 2025 OR y EQUALS 2026
                    THEN `s 2013(a)(2)(A) the payment error rate of the State for the fiscal year` rates y
                OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the election is of "the payment error rate of the State from fiscal year 2025 or 2026"

-- src:158 | For fiscal year 2029 and each fiscal year thereafter, to calculate the applicable State share under clause (i), the Secretary shall use the payment error rate of the State for the third fiscal year preceding the fiscal year for which the State share is being calculated.
@ref s 2013(a)(2)(B)(ii)(II), fiscal year 2029 and thereafter (src:158)
GIVEN rates IS A LIST OF `s 2013(a)(2) payment error rate of a year`
      `the fiscal year for which the State share is being calculated` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(ii)(II) the payment error rate the Secretary uses for fiscal year 2029 and each fiscal year thereafter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the fiscal year for which the State share is being calculated` LESS THAN 2029
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the clause is for "fiscal year 2029 and each fiscal year thereafter"
        OTHERWISE `s 2013(a)(2)(A) the payment error rate of the State for the fiscal year` rates (`the fiscal year for which the State share is being calculated` MINUS 3)  -- "the payment error rate of the State for the third fiscal year preceding the fiscal year for which the State share is being calculated"

-- src:161 | If, for fiscal year 2025, the payment error rate of a State multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent, the implementation date under clause (i) for that State shall be fiscal year 2029.
@ref s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii)(I), the 1.5 times test for a rate (src:161)
GIVEN rate IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii) the payment error rate multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent` MEANS
    CONSIDER rate
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the payment error rate for the year was not supplied
        WHEN JUST x THEN JUST ((x TIMES 1.5) AT LEAST 20)

-- src:161 | If, for fiscal year 2025, the payment error rate of a State multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent, the implementation date under clause (i) for that State shall be fiscal year 2029.
-- src:162 | (II) Fiscal year 2026
-- src:163 | If, for fiscal year 2026, the payment error rate of a State multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent, the implementation date under clause (i) for that State shall be fiscal year 2030.
@ref s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii), delayed implementation (src:161-163)
GIVEN `the payment error rate of the State for fiscal year 2025` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the payment error rate of the State for fiscal year 2026` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii) the fiscal year in which the implementation date under clause (i) falls` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` (`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii) the payment error rate multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent` `the payment error rate of the State for fiscal year 2025`)
           AND `snap1 is definitely yes` (`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii) the payment error rate multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent` `the payment error rate of the State for fiscal year 2026`)
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subclause (I) makes the date fiscal year 2029 and subclause (II) makes it fiscal year 2030, and the clause does not say which governs a State that meets both
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` (`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii) the payment error rate multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent` `the payment error rate of the State for fiscal year 2026`)
           AND `snap1 is definitely no` (`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii) the payment error rate multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent` `the payment error rate of the State for fiscal year 2025`)
            THEN JUST 2030  -- the text says yes: "If, for fiscal year 2026, the payment error rate of a State multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent, the implementation date under clause (i) for that State shall be fiscal year 2030"
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` (`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii) the payment error rate multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent` `the payment error rate of the State for fiscal year 2025`)
           AND `snap1 is definitely no` (`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii) the payment error rate multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent` `the payment error rate of the State for fiscal year 2026`)
            THEN JUST 2029  -- the text says yes: "If, for fiscal year 2025, the payment error rate of a State multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent, the implementation date under clause (i) for that State shall be fiscal year 2029"
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` (`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii) the payment error rate multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent` `the payment error rate of the State for fiscal year 2025`)
           AND `snap1 is definitely no` (`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(iii) the payment error rate multiplied by 1.5 is equal to or above 20 percent` `the payment error rate of the State for fiscal year 2026`)
            THEN JUST 2028  -- the date of clause (i): "beginning in fiscal year 2028"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a payment error rate that decides the implementation date was not supplied

-- src:150 | (I) less than 6 percent, the Federal share of the cost of the allotment described in paragraph (1) for that State in a fiscal year shall be 100 percent, and the State share shall be 0 percent;
-- src:151 | (II) equal to or greater than 6 percent but less than 8 percent, the Federal share of the cost of the allotment described in paragraph (1) for that State in a fiscal year shall be 95 percent, and the State share shall be 5 percent;
-- src:152 | (III) equal to or greater than 8 percent but less than 10 percent, the Federal share of the cost of the allotment described in paragraph (1) for that State in a fiscal year shall be 90 percent, and the State share shall be 10 percent; and
-- src:153 | (IV) equal to or greater than 10 percent, the Federal share of the cost of the allotment described in paragraph (1) for that State in a fiscal year shall be 85 percent, and the State share shall be 15 percent.
@ref s 2013(a)(2)(B)(i), the four shares (src:150-153)
GIVEN rate IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `s 2013(a)(2) shares`
`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(i) the shares for the payment error rate` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF rate LESS THAN 6
            THEN `s 2013(a)(2) shares` WITH
                    `s 2013(a)(2) the Federal share of the cost of the allotment, in percent` IS 100
                    `s 2013(a)(2) the State share of the cost of the allotment, in percent` IS 0
        IF rate LESS THAN 8
            THEN `s 2013(a)(2) shares` WITH
                    `s 2013(a)(2) the Federal share of the cost of the allotment, in percent` IS 95
                    `s 2013(a)(2) the State share of the cost of the allotment, in percent` IS 5
        IF rate LESS THAN 10
            THEN `s 2013(a)(2) shares` WITH
                    `s 2013(a)(2) the Federal share of the cost of the allotment, in percent` IS 90
                    `s 2013(a)(2) the State share of the cost of the allotment, in percent` IS 10
        OTHERWISE `s 2013(a)(2) shares` WITH
                    `s 2013(a)(2) the Federal share of the cost of the allotment, in percent` IS 85
                    `s 2013(a)(2) the State share of the cost of the allotment, in percent` IS 15

-- src:149 | Subject to clause (iii), beginning in fiscal year 2028, if the payment error rate of a State as determined under clause (ii) is—
@ref s 2013(a)(2)(B)(i), in general (src:149)
GIVEN `the fiscal year` IS A NUMBER
      `the fiscal year in which the implementation date under clause (i) falls` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the payment error rate as determined under clause (ii)` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 2013(a)(2) shares`
`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(i) the shares of the cost of the allotment for the State in the fiscal year` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the fiscal year in which the implementation date under clause (i) falls`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the implementation date, which clause (iii) can move, was not determined
        WHEN JUST implementation THEN
            BRANCH
                IF `the fiscal year` LESS THAN implementation
                    THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the shares are for the fiscal years "beginning in fiscal year 2028", or from the later implementation date under clause (iii)
                OTHERWISE
                    CONSIDER `the payment error rate as determined under clause (ii)`
                        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the payment error rate as determined under clause (ii) was not supplied
                        WHEN JUST r THEN JUST (`s 2013(a)(2)(B)(i) the shares for the payment error rate` r)

-- src:165 | The Secretary may not pay towards the cost of an allotment described in paragraph (1) an amount that is greater than the applicable Federal share under paragraph (2).
@ref s 2013(a)(3), maximum Federal payment (src:165)
GIVEN `the amount the Secretary would pay, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the cost of the allotment, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
      `the applicable Federal share, in percent` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2013(a)(3) the Secretary may pay the amount towards the cost of the allotment` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the amount the Secretary would pay, in dollars` GREATER THAN (`the cost of the allotment, in dollars` TIMES (`the applicable Federal share, in percent` DIVIDED BY 100))
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary may not pay towards the cost of an allotment ... an amount that is greater than the applicable Federal share"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is a ceiling; it does not authorize a payment up to it

§ `s 2013(b) Food distribution program on Indian reservations`

-- src:168 | Distribution of commodities, with or without the supplemental nutrition assistance program, shall be made whenever a request for concurrent or separate food program operations, respectively, is made by a tribal organization.
@ref s 2013(b)(1) (src:168)
GIVEN `a tribal organization has made a request for concurrent or separate food program operations` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2013(b)(1) the distribution of commodities shall be made` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a tribal organization has made a request for concurrent or separate food program operations`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "Distribution of commodities, with or without the supplemental nutrition assistance program, shall be made whenever a request ... is made by a tribal organization"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "shall be made whenever a request for concurrent or separate food program operations, respectively, is made by a tribal organization" (a failed "whenever", read as "if", marginal reading (a))

-- src:173 | If the Secretary determines that a tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently administering a distribution described in paragraph (1), then the tribal organization shall administer the distribution.
@ref s 2013(b)(2)(B) (src:173)
GIVEN `the Secretary determines that the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently administering a distribution described in paragraph (1)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2013(b)(2)(B) the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently administering the distribution` MEANS
    `the Secretary determines that the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently administering a distribution described in paragraph (1)`  -- the Secretary's determination, passed through as the answer. NOTHING means the caller does not know; a caller who knows the Secretary has NOT determined the organization capable (found it not capable, or made no finding) passes JUST FALSE, and the rule below then names the State agency

-- src:171 | Subject to subparagraphs (B) and (C), in the event of distribution on all or part of an Indian reservation, the appropriate agency of the State government in the area involved shall be responsible for the distribution.
-- src:172 | (B) Administration by tribal organization
-- src:173 | If the Secretary determines that a tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently administering a distribution described in paragraph (1), then the tribal organization shall administer the distribution.
@ref s 2013(b)(2)(A) and (B), who administers (src:171-173)
GIVEN `the distribution is on all or part of an Indian reservation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 2013(b)(2)(B) the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently administering the distribution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE Party
`s 2013(b)(2) the party that administers the distribution` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF NOT `the distribution is on all or part of an Indian reservation`
            THEN NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (2)(A) is "in the event of distribution on all or part of an Indian reservation"
        IF `snap1 is definitely yes` `s 2013(b)(2)(B) the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently administering the distribution`
            THEN JUST `a tribal organization`  -- "then the tribal organization shall administer the distribution"
        IF `snap1 is definitely no` `s 2013(b)(2)(B) the tribal organization is capable of effectively and efficiently administering the distribution`
            THEN JUST `the State agency`  -- "the appropriate agency of the State government in the area involved shall be responsible for the distribution" (subparagraph (B) not triggered: a failed "if", marginal reading (a))
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the Secretary has determined the organization capable under subparagraph (B) is not known (a caller who knows there is no determination passes JUST FALSE)

-- src:175 | The Secretary shall not approve any plan for a distribution described in paragraph (1) that permits any household on any Indian reservation to participate simultaneously in the supplemental nutrition assistance program and the program established under this subsection.
@ref s 2013(b)(2)(C) (src:175)
GIVEN `the plan permits a household on an Indian reservation to participate simultaneously in the supplemental nutrition assistance program and the program established under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2013(b)(2)(C) the Secretary may approve the plan` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the plan permits a household on an Indian reservation to participate simultaneously in the supplemental nutrition assistance program and the program established under subsection (b)`
            THEN JUST FALSE  -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The Secretary shall not approve any plan for a distribution described in paragraph (1) that permits any household on any Indian reservation to participate simultaneously in the supplemental nutrition assistance program and the program established under this subsection"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the bar is on a plan "that permits any household on any Indian reservation to participate simultaneously"

-- src:177 | An individual who is disqualified from participation in the food distribution program on Indian reservations under this subsection is not eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under this chapter for a period of time to be determined by the Secretary.
@ref s 2013(b)(3) (src:177)
GIVEN `the individual is disqualified from participation in the food distribution program on Indian reservations under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `Period of ineligibility`
`s 2013(b)(3) the period for which the individual is not eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the individual is disqualified from participation in the food distribution program on Indian reservations under subsection (b)`
            THEN JUST `for a period the Secretary prescribes by regulation, not stated in this text`  -- "for a period of time to be determined by the Secretary"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the sentence is for "an individual who is disqualified from participation in the food distribution program on Indian reservations"

-- src:177 | An individual who is disqualified from participation in the food distribution program on Indian reservations under this subsection is not eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under this chapter for a period of time to be determined by the Secretary.
@ref s 2013(b)(3), the ineligibility (src:177)
GIVEN `the individual is disqualified from participation in the food distribution program on Indian reservations under subsection (b)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the period determined by the Secretary has not ended` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 2013(b)(3) the individual is not eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the individual is disqualified from participation in the food distribution program on Indian reservations under subsection (b)` AND `snap1 is definitely yes` `the period determined by the Secretary has not ended`
            THEN JUST TRUE  -- the text says yes: "is not eligible to participate in the supplemental nutrition assistance program under this chapter for a period of time to be determined by the Secretary"
        OTHERWISE NOTHING  -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the ineligibility is "for a period of time to be determined by the Secretary", and the period or the disqualification is not shown to run

-- src:180 | Subject to subparagraph (B), the Secretary shall pay not less than 80 percent of administrative costs and distribution costs on Indian reservations as the Secretary determines necessary for effective administration of such distribution by a State agency or tribal organization.
@ref s 2013(b)(4)(A) (src:180)
GIVEN `the administrative costs and distribution costs on Indian reservations that the Secretary determines necessary for effective administration of the distribution by a State agency or tribal organization, in dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 2013(b)(4)(A) the least amount the Secretary must pay` MEANS
    0.8 TIMES `the administrative costs and distribution costs on Indian reservations that the Secretary determines necessary for effective administration of the distribution by a State agency or tribal organization, in dollars`

-- src:182 | The Secretary shall waive up to 100 percent of the non-Federal share of the costs described in subparagraph (A) if the Secretary determines that—
-- src:183 | (i) the tribal organization is financially unable to provide a greater non-Federal share of the costs; or
-- src:184 | (ii) providing a greater non-Federal share of the costs would be a substantial burden for the tribal organization.
@ref s 2013(b)(4)(B), waiver (src:182-184)
GIVEN `the tribal organization is financially unable to provide a greater non-Federal share of the costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `providing a greater non-Federal share of the costs would be a substantial burden for the tribal organization` IS A BOOLEAN
